From 729371e624575e8779a587fba5593640681b4303 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:53:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): scope managed-worker credentials to adopted
 executions [daveey]

Managed-child exec inherited profile-wide credentials after environment scrubbing;
the bootstrap also serialized the route API key and inline policy secrets.
Replace inheritance with a positive startup allowlist and keep credential material
owner-side until the exact execution adopts through authenticated worker RPC.

Why: scrub-then-overlay reintroduced every profile secret. Inherited exec env also
made single-profile workers bypass the isolation boundary. Bootstrap mixed launch
policy and private values. Existing tests asserted that propagation instead of
least privilege. Execution-scoped owner resolution now preserves selected route
keys without either bootstrap disclosure or blanket environment inheritance.

Proof (synthetic credentials only):
- RED: test_managed_worker_least_privilege.py initially had 4 failures on main
  83a5d885d574662fd5cff0493fb702f8203e4405: positive exec boundary (single/multiplex),
  bound launch-key bootstrap and inline-config bootstrap.
- Additional RED: 5 selected-provider regressions exposed OpenRouter, auto/default,
  bare-custom and provider-alias compatibility gaps in the first implementation.
- GREEN: focused canonical runner passes least-privilege, managed turn contract,
  route key, profile env, exec boundary, worker admission, frozen safe-policy,
  Desktop completion-obligation and serve-handler ledger suites, no file retries.
- Full gateway sweep and fresh-base checks pending before publication/landing.

No real credentials inspected. No Example runtime or unit changes.
